&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Paid Media Director, you will lead paid media strategy, performance, and client relationships across complex consumer acquisition programs, with a focus on Telehealth and digital health. You will lead cross-functional teams while staying close to the platforms, performance data, measurement and business economics required to drive profitable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires deep paid media expertise combined with an understanding of what makes Telehealth and digital health acquisition different: advertising and data-use restrictions, privacy-constrained measurement, complex patient journeys, and the need to connect media acquisition to downstream patient and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and execution of integrated paid media strategies across paid social, paid search, display, video, and emerging platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own senior client relationships, translating business objectives, customer economics, and growth goals into clear media strategies, measurement frameworks, testing roadmaps, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead paid media strategy for Telehealth and regulated healthcare businesses, navigating platform policies, privacy and data-use restrictions, measurement constraints, and business economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee media planning, forecasting, performance and investment decisions, using acquisition efficiency, incrementally, and business economics to guide budget allocation and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose performance beyond the media account, identifying how creative, conversion experiences, patient flows, measurement, product, and economics may enable or constrain growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish structured testing approaches across media, creative, targeting, offers, and conversion experiences, including environments with restricted targeting or limited conversion signals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop teams of media buyers and strategists, establishing high standards for strategic thinking, execution, analytical rigor, and client service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep platform fluency and step into campaign structure, optimization, tracking, and performance detail when needed to guide teams and troubleshoot challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve team processes, operating standards, and ways of working to support quality, scalability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on changes in healthcare advertising policies, privacy and data-use requirements, measurement practices, and advertising platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Must currently live in New York City.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of paid media or performance marketing experience, including significant agency experience and senior-level ownership of complex consumer acquisition programs, and at least 2 years of experience with Telehealth businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading paid media strategy for Telehealth, digital health, or similarly regulated healthcare businesses. Direct-to-consumer Telehealth experience is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Telehealth patient acquisition journeys and how media connects to downstream clinical, customer, and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep cross-channel expertise across paid social, paid search, display, video, and other relevant media channels, particularly Meta and Google.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of healthcare advertising and data-use restrictions and their implications for targeting, optimization, creative, conversion tracking, and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of acquisition economics, including CAC, contribution margin, retention/LTV, and payback, and the ability to connect media performance to broader business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing meaningful media budgets and complex, cross-channel acquisition programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success managing and developing high-performing media teams through coaching, training and clear performance standards, while leading senior-level client relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic, analytical, and commercial thinking, with the ability to turn complex performance and business data into clear recommendations and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership and communication skills, with experience working across analytics, creative, product, engineering, legal/compliance, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
